+PDM/DMIC Devicetree Configuration Demo
+======================================
+
+This directory contains a demonstration of how to use the new devicetree macros
+for PDM/DMIC configuration.
+
+New Macros
+----------
+
+1. PDM_DT_IO_CFG_GET(node_id)
+   - Returns a struct pdm_io_cfg initialized from devicetree properties
+   - Requires: clk-frequency-min, clk-frequency-max, clk-duty-cycle-min, clk-duty-cycle-max
+
+2. PDM_DT_HAS_LEFT_CHANNEL(node_id)
+   - Returns 1 if the node has the channel-left property
+   - Returns 0 otherwise
+
+3. PDM_DT_HAS_RIGHT_CHANNEL(node_id)
+   - Returns 1 if the node has the channel-right property
+   - Returns 0 otherwise
+
+Devicetree Requirements
+------------------------
+
+A devicetree node using compatible "zephyr,pdm-dmic" should have:
+
+- clk-frequency-min: minimum PDM clock frequency (uint32_t)
+- clk-frequency-max: maximum PDM clock frequency (uint32_t)  
+- clk-duty-cycle-min: minimum duty cycle in % (uint8_t)
+- clk-duty-cycle-max: maximum duty cycle in % (uint8_t)
+- channel-left: (optional) indicates left channel is available
+- channel-right: (optional) indicates right channel is available
+
+Example Devicetree Node
+------------------------
+
+/ {
+    my_mic: pdm-mic@12340000 {
+        compatible = "zephyr,pdm-dmic";
+        clk-frequency-min = <1000000>;
+        clk-frequency-max = <3500000>;
+        clk-duty-cycle-min = <40>;
+        clk-duty-cycle-max = <60>;
+        channel-left;
+        channel-right;
+    };
+};
+
+Example Usage
+-------------
+
+#include <zephyr/audio/dmic.h>
+#include <zephyr/devicetree.h>
+
+#define MY_MIC_NODE DT_NODELABEL(my_mic)
+
+void setup_mic(void)
+{
+    struct pdm_io_cfg io_cfg;
+    struct dmic_cfg dmic_cfg;
+    
+    /* Get IO configuration from devicetree */
+    io_cfg = PDM_DT_IO_CFG_GET(MY_MIC_NODE);
+    
+    /* Check available channels */
+    bool has_left = PDM_DT_HAS_LEFT_CHANNEL(MY_MIC_NODE);
+    bool has_right = PDM_DT_HAS_RIGHT_CHANNEL(MY_MIC_NODE);
+    
+    /* Use the configuration */
+    dmic_cfg.io = io_cfg;
+    /* ... configure other fields ... */
+}
